    58	## Adopted implementation
    59	
    60	- D155: reference lists no longer veto candidates; full-match period handling, exact scopes, event identity, same-answer coalescing, old-key trust and atomic write and resume.
    61	- D159: an item's accepted extraction answers the request built after every earlier item finished writing.
    62	- D172, D181, D183: the parallel day (`hivemind.parallel_day`), the replay's default (`scripts/replay.py --workers 1` runs serially): later items' extraction requests are prepared early and prepared again right after any commit that changes them; each item accepts only a byte-identical request at its turn; matching questions within an item run concurrently and apply in order; one writer.
    63	- D163–D166: the English runtime (`vocabulary.py`, canonical values with legacy conversion on read), the fresh English library, research groups declared during extraction with aliases and decided by names in code (`views/groups.py`).
    64	- D167–D169: no hard-coded identity; the measure vocabulary gains `market_size` and `project_cost`; the Jev engine (`views/jev_matching.py`, client `jev.py`) with the PRD's replacement definition, the shared succession rule and an answer for "the same quantity, another period"; a repeat may name the piece shown for the same evidence under another thesis.
    65	- Idea service: the adopted two-call contract `poc-v9` / `idea-v7`, reasoning `none` (D135/D145); limits in the [Idea specification](poc/idea-card.md). The service still reads the sealed Chinese ledger with its search index.
    66	- UI and service: shared thesis schema and adapter, cards, history chart, evidence, drawer and graph routing; historical reads, search, numeric claim evaluation and thesis bundles over HTTP and MCP ([service specification](poc/service.md)).
    67	- D207–D211: extraction reads, then files (`extraction.read_item`, `extraction.file_reading`); under a ledger-blind version the request depends on the item alone, so the parallel day prepares the read early and files it at the item's turn; the placement call files statements, and a statement filed nowhere is dropped as `no home` (the `unplaced_statements` table is retired). After placement the sift's candidate rule runs again (`extraction.candidates_with_evidence`): a candidate left with none of its evidence is dropped, so no thesis opens without evidence (close-out review; 0 of 222 candidates under poc-v67, 25 of 5,805 over all stored loop answers).
    68	- D236: a quote that differs from the source only by punctuation, quotation marks, footnote markers or case, or leaves out one run of words inside one sentence, is stored as the exact source passage (`extraction.repair_quote`); anything else is refused.
    69	- The year rule reads the universe's year forms (`universe.parse_year`, so FY29 is FY2029) and counts a fiscal year in the company's own fiscal years (`universe.fiscal_year_of`, shared with the fiscal note; NVIDIA's FY2028 in July 2026 is next year); an event question that names its quarter is not a quarterly number.
    70	- role-v13..v15 alone name `shared_quantity`; every later prompt version gets the current four opening reasons with no code change (`extraction.SHARED_QUANTITY_VERSIONS`).
    71	- Tests read no credential: `tests/conftest.py` makes the model and Jev key readers refuse, and the collision judge sends with the caller's transport.
    72	- Preflight (`scripts/preflight.py`) verifies each stored extraction request against its archived configuration and source (the first `MAX_TEXT_CHARS` characters, as production sends) before replaying its answer through the current checks; a request it cannot rebuild (a Chinese version, v17's paragraph accounts) is counted and named, not fatal; the item header is one function (`extraction.item_header`).
    73	- The placement setting is checked before the paid extraction call; the credential guard in tests raises `pytest.fail`, which the pipeline's `except Exception` cannot swallow.
